{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The expression for $g(x)$ includes $\\sin(x)$.\n\nRemember that the derivative of $\\sin(x)$ is $\\cos(x)$.\n\nPut another way, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\sin(x)]=\\cos(x)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\ng'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}[5x^2+4\\sin(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^2)+4\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\sin(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5\\cdot2x+4\\cdot\\cos(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=10x+4\\cos(x)\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$g'(x)=10x+4\\cos(x)$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $g(x)=5x^2+4\\sin(x)$.\n\n$g'(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"10x+4\\cos\\left(x\\right)"}],"buttonSets":["basic","trig"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
